proposed_statement_changes.proposed:
Remove the remaining at-most-\(\log(ed)\) gap in the proved same-class characterization
\[
 c_\epsilon L_{n,d}\leq R_{n,d,\epsilon}
 \leq C_\epsilon\log(ed)L_{n,d}
\]
for every \(n\geq1\) and \(d\geq2\).  Specifically, determine an explicit numerical function \(\rho(n,d)\), not defined by a minimax optimization, fully specify a measurable probability-valued estimator \(\widehat G_{\mathrm{grp}}\) by instantiating or replacing the candidate blueprint in \(\mathrm{def:grouped\mbox{-}reconstruction\mbox{-}handle}\), and prove a matching converse on \(\mathcal M_{d,\epsilon}\) such that
\[
 c_\epsilon\rho(n,d)\leq R_{n,d,\epsilon}
 \leq \sup_{P\in\mathcal M_{d,\epsilon}}
 E_{P^n}\!\left[W_1(\widehat G_{\mathrm{grp}},G_P)^2\right]
 \leq C_\epsilon\rho(n,d).
\]
The answer must determine which elbows in \(\mathrm{prop:lower\mbox{-}benchmark\mbox{-}phase\mbox{-}diagram}\) are genuine, give the exact consistency region, reproduce the \(d/n\) lower bound on the separated-atom hypercube, and yield a nonconstant guarantee for two effect clusters with unknown unequal masses and propensities at both overlap boundaries.

